<title>CANADA: Canada names new G7 &quot;sherpa&quot;.</title>
<headline>Canada names new G7 &quot;sherpa&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Jean Chretien announced on Wednesday he had appointed Donald Campbell, Canada's ambassador to Japan, as his new &quot;sherpa&quot; for Group of Seven summit meetings.</p>
<p>Campbell, who will be a deputy foreign minister, replaces Gordon Smith, who is retiring. The so-called sherpas are top officials of each G7 country who prepare policy documents for the annual summits.</p>
</text>
